  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records collectively establish temperature-dependent mechanical testing and molecular-dynamics deformation of HEAs, coating tribology and hardness measurements, dislocation-mediated strengthening, temperature-driven changes between stacking-fault/twinning and other deformation modes, FCC-HCP transformation, and order-disorder evolution. R8 and R9 provide the strongest mechanistic pointers, while R1 and R18 connect coatings with hardness or tribological behavior. However, none describes temperature-controlled nanoindentation and friction MD for an FCC FeNiCrCoCu film on Cu, nor the specific stable-to-600 K followed by disorder-driven softening above about 900 K. Reconstructing that combined intervention and threshold behavior would therefore require a substantial new design step."
